# Never: a plaintext credential, sitting inside a directory that is committed as the paper's artefact.
.pwd

# Build outputs and third-party downloads, not sources. `build.sh` regenerates the package; the benchmark
# archives are repackaged TPTP problems; `sec/` is the official StarExecCommand client.
#
# Every archive, by extension rather than by name. The list used to be per name -- `lisaST.tgz`, `dryrun*.tgz`
# and so on -- and each new package built for a job (`lisaST-e1`, `lisaST-full`, `lisaST-single`, `probe`)
# fell outside it and was committed: six of them, about 300 MB, each one a jar plus the axiom files that
# `build.sh` reassembles from `$TPTP` in a couple of minutes. Nothing here is a source.
*.tgz
*.zip
sec/
